IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001 (Cth) -- Part 2, as the individual meets it: what ASIC is for
-- (ss 11(1), 12A(1)-(2)); Division 2, consumer protection in financial services: what counts as a financial service
-- (s 12BAB(1), (1AA), (7), (9)) and acquiring one as a consumer (s 12BC(1)-(3)); unfair terms in consumer and small business
-- contracts (ss 12BF(1), (3)-(4), 12BG(1), (4), 12BI(1)(a)-(c), (f), 12BL(1)); unconscionable conduct (s 12CB(1)-(2)); misleading or
-- deceptive conduct (ss 12BB(1), 12DA(1), (1A)); harassment and coercion (s 12DJ); unsolicited credit and debit cards (s 12DL(1),
-- (2)); unsolicited financial services (ss 12DM(1), 12DMA); the implied warranties (ss 12EB(1), 12EC, 12ED(1)-(3)); damages
-- (s 12GF(1), (1B), (2)); penalties (ss 12GB(1), 12GBA(6), 12GBCA(1)-(2)); and, from Part 3, what ASIC may require of the founder
-- in an investigation (ss 13(1), (6), 19, 23(1), 30(1), 63(1), (5), 68).
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom Part 2 is applied -- the consumer of financial services (a borrower, a cardholder, a person
-- chased for a debt), and the company founder as far as Daniel's registration of Jarrah needs: the founder issuing shares
-- to an investor, the founder whose small company signs a bank's standard terms, and the founder ASIC may examine. "What may
-- not be done to me, what do I get, and what can ASIC make me do?". Where the Act addresses the supplier ("a person must not")
-- it is encoded as what may be done to the individual. Where the Act hands a judgment to a court (misleading, unconscionable,
-- "significant imbalance", "undue harassment", "not fair or reasonable") it is asked as a fact.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 109, compilation date 19 September 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 87, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00429, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00819.txt. No regulations are deposited: the "greater amount"
-- that may be prescribed for s 12BC(3)(a)(ii) and the value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA) are INPUTS.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Part 2 Division 1 beyond ss 11(1) and 12A(1)-(2) (constitution, membership, Ministerial directions, APRA);
-- the definition of "financial product" (s 12BAA) beyond being asked as a fact; s 12BC(3)(b)-(e) (how the price is worked out
-- for mixed supplies and credit: the price is an input); s 12BG(2) (matters the court weighs), s 12BH (examples of unfair terms),
-- s 12BI(1)(d)-(e), s 12BK (the standard form presumption: an input), ss 12BL(1A)-(4), 12BLA-12BLC; s 12CA (the unwritten law);
-- s 12CC (matters the court may weigh); ss 12DB-12DI, 12DK, 12DMB, 12DMC, 12DN; Subdivision DA (add-on insurance); ss 12EA,
-- 12ED(2A); Subdivision G beyond the provisions named (injunctions, non-party redress, orders for unfair terms, infringement
-- notices, substantiation notices, proportionate liability); Part 3 beyond the provisions named; Parts 3A onwards (the
-- Takeovers Panel, the Financial Reporting Council, the Parliamentary Joint Committee, confidentiality, fees). Registration of
-- the company itself is the Corporations Act 2001's (s 117), not this Act's; the share placement's disclosure exemption is
-- Corporations Act s 708. "Financial product", "body corporate", "eligible person", "in trade or commerce" and the Corporations
-- Act provisions in s 12DA(1A) are borrowed or applied terms, asked as facts.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `ASIC Act 2001 -- Part 2 from the seat of the consumer of financial services and the founder`

§§ `ss 11, 12A -- what ASIC does with my company and my financial dealings`

-- s 11(1): "ASIC has such functions and powers as are conferred on it by or under the corporations legislation (other than the
-- excluded provisions)." s 12A(1): ASIC "has the functions and powers that are conferred on it by or under Division 2 of Part 2
-- of this Act" and by the Acts listed, among them "(i) the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009" and "(k) the Business
-- Names Registration Act 2011". s 12A(2): "the function of monitoring and promoting market integrity and consumer protection in
-- relation to the Australian financial system." Gloss: the ASIC Act gives ASIC no registration power of its own; it points to
-- the Acts that do.
DECLARE `What I am dealing with` IS ONE OF
    `registering or running a company`
    `registering a business name`
    `consumer credit`
    `other financial services`
    `something outside the financial system`

DECLARE `Where ASIC's role comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the corporations legislation (s 11(1)); registration is under the Corporations Act`
    `the Business Names Registration Act 2011 (s 12A(1)(k))`
    `the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 (s 12A(1)(i)) and Part 2 Division 2`
    `Part 2 Division 2 and the consumer protection function (s 12A(1), (2))`
    `no function of ASIC under ss 11 or 12A`

@export Where does ASIC's role in what I am doing come from (ss 11(1), 12A(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `What I am dealing with` @desc What you are doing: registering a company, a business name, consumer credit, other financial services, or something else
GIVETH A `Where ASIC's role comes from`
DECIDE `Where does ASIC's role come from` IS
    CONSIDER `what I am doing`
    WHEN `registering or running a company` THEN `the corporations legislation (s 11(1)); registration is under the Corporations Act`
    WHEN `registering a business name` THEN `the Business Names Registration Act 2011 (s 12A(1)(k))`
    WHEN `consumer credit` THEN `the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 (s 12A(1)(i)) and Part 2 Division 2`
    WHEN `other financial services` THEN `Part 2 Division 2 and the consumer protection function (s 12A(1), (2))`
    OTHERWISE `no function of ASIC under ss 11 or 12A`

§§ `s 12BAB -- is what the other side does a financial service`

-- s 12BAB(1): a person provides a financial service if they "(a) provide financial product advice ...; or (b) deal in a
-- financial product ...", or (c)-(h) make a market, operate a registered scheme, provide a custodial or depository service, a
-- superannuation trustee service, a claims handling and settling service, operate a market or clearing facility, or "provide a
-- service ... that is otherwise supplied in relation to a financial product". (1AA): "a financial product is a financial
-- service". (7): dealing is "(a) applying for or acquiring a financial product; (b) issuing a financial product; ... (d)
-- varying ...; (e) disposing of a financial product." (9): "A person is taken not to deal in a financial product if the person
-- deals in the product on their own behalf, unless: (a) the person is an issuer of financial products; and (b) the dealing is
-- in relation to one or more of those products." Gloss: "financial product" (s 12BAA) is asked as a fact; s 12BAA(4) Note 1
-- gives shares issued by a company as an example of a financial investment.
DECLARE `What the other side does` HAS
    `the thing supplied is itself a financial product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gives financial product advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applies for, acquires, issues, varies or disposes of a financial product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `does so only on its own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the issuer of the product dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN
    `does another thing listed in s 12BAB(1)(c)-(h)` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is what is being done a financial service under the ASIC Act (s 12BAB)?
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `What the other side does` @desc What is being supplied or done, and on whose behalf
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a financial service` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the thing supplied is itself a financial product`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `gives financial product advice`
    OR  (    `the conduct`'s `applies for, acquires, issues, varies or disposes of a financial product`
         AND (   (NOT `the conduct`'s `does so only on its own behalf`)
              OR `the conduct`'s `is the issuer of the product dealt in`))
    OR  `the conduct`'s `does another thing listed in s 12BAB(1)(c)-(h)`

§§ `s 12BC -- did I acquire the financial services as a consumer`

-- s 12BC(1): a person acquired financial services as a consumer "if, and only if: (a) the price of the services did not exceed
-- the prescribed amount; or (b) if the price ... exceeded the prescribed amount--the services were of a kind ordinarily
-- acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption; or (c) if the services were acquired for use or consumption
-- in connection with a small business ... and the price ... exceeded the prescribed amount--the services were of a kind
-- ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption." (2): "small business means a business employing less than: (a) if the
-- business is or includes the manufacture of goods--100 people; or (b) otherwise--20 people." (3)(a): "the prescribed amount
-- is: (i) $40,000; or (ii) if a greater amount is prescribed ...--that greater amount". No regulation is deposited, so the
-- greater amount is an input (0 if none). (4): a person alleged to be a consumer is presumed one unless the contrary is shown.
`the amount in s 12BC(3)(a)(i)` MEANS 40000

@export What is the most the financial services can cost and still be acquired as a consumer whatever their kind (s 12BC(3)(a))?
GIVEN `a greater amount prescribed by regulation` IS A NUMBER @desc Any greater amount the regulations prescribe for s 12BC(3)(a)(ii), in dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the s 12BC prescribed amount` IS
    IF `a greater amount prescribed by regulation` GREATER THAN `the amount in s 12BC(3)(a)(i)`
    THEN `a greater amount prescribed by regulation`
    ELSE `the amount in s 12BC(3)(a)(i)`

@export Is my business a small business for s 12BC (s 12BC(2))?
GIVEN `people my business employs` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people your business employs
      `my business is or includes manufacturing goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business is or includes the manufacture of goods
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my business a small business under s 12BC` IF
    IF `my business is or includes manufacturing goods`
    THEN `people my business employs` LESS THAN 100
    ELSE `people my business employs` LESS THAN 20

DECLARE `My acquisition of financial services` HAS
    `price` IS A NUMBER
    `a greater prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired for use in connection with my small business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Did I acquire the financial services as a consumer (s 12BC(1))?
GIVEN `what I acquired` IS A `My acquisition of financial services` @desc The financial services you acquired, their price, and their kind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I acquire the financial services as a consumer` IF
        `what I acquired`'s `price` AT MOST `What is the s 12BC prescribed amount` (`what I acquired`'s `a greater prescribed amount`)
    OR  `what I acquired`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use or consumption`
    OR  (    `what I acquired`'s `acquired for use in connection with my small business`
         AND `what I acquired`'s `of a kind ordinarily acquired for business use or consumption`)

§§ `ss 12BF-12BL -- is a term of my contract void as unfair`

-- s 12BF(3): "A consumer contract is a contract at least one of the parties to which is an individual whose acquisition of
-- what is supplied under the contract is wholly or predominantly an acquisition for personal, domestic or household use or
-- consumption." (4): a small business contract if "(a) the upfront price payable under the contract does not exceed
-- $5,000,000; and (b) at least one party ... (i) ... makes the contract in the course of carrying on a business and at a time
-- when the party employs fewer than 100 persons; (ii) the party's turnover ... for the party's last income year ... is less
-- than $10,000,000." The head-count under (6) (casuals only if regular and systematic, part-timers as fractions) is an input.
`the upfront price limit in s 12BF(4)(a)` MEANS 5000000
`the head-count limit in s 12BF(4)(b)(i)` MEANS 100
`the turnover limit in s 12BF(4)(b)(ii)` MEANS 10000000

DECLARE `The party` HAS
    `contracts in the course of carrying on a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `persons employed, counted under s 12BF(6)` IS A NUMBER
    `turnover for its last income year` IS A NUMBER

@export Is my contract a small business contract (s 12BF(4))?
GIVEN `the upfront price` IS A NUMBER @desc The upfront price payable under the contract, in dollars, leaving out interest on credit (s 12BF(5))
      `my business` IS A `The party` @desc Your business: whether it contracts in the course of business, its head-count and its turnover
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a small business contract` IF
        `the upfront price` AT MOST `the upfront price limit in s 12BF(4)(a)`
    AND (    (    `my business`'s `contracts in the course of carrying on a business`
              AND `my business`'s `persons employed, counted under s 12BF(6)` LESS THAN `the head-count limit in s 12BF(4)(b)(i)`)
         OR  `my business`'s `turnover for its last income year` LESS THAN `the turnover limit in s 12BF(4)(b)(ii)`)

-- s 12BG(1): "A term ... is unfair if: (a) it would cause a significant imbalance in the parties' rights and obligations
-- arising under the contract; and (b) it is not reasonably necessary in order to protect the legitimate interests of the party
-- who would be advantaged by the term; and (c) it would cause detriment (whether financial or otherwise) to a party if it were
-- to be applied or relied on." (4): a term "is presumed not to be reasonably necessary ... unless that party proves otherwise".
DECLARE `The term` HAS
    `causes a significant imbalance in rights and obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the advantaged party proved it reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would cause me detriment if applied or relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
    `defines the main subject matter of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets the upfront price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is required or expressly permitted by a law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a transparent insurance excess disclosed before the contract` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the term unfair (s 12BG(1), (4))?
GIVEN `the term` IS A `The term` @desc The term, its effect, and what the advantaged party has proved
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term unfair` IF
        `the term`'s `causes a significant imbalance in rights and obligations`
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `the advantaged party proved it reasonably necessary to protect its legitimate interests`)
    AND `the term`'s `would cause me detriment if applied or relied on`

-- s 12BF(1): "A term of a consumer contract or small business contract is void if: (a) the term is unfair; and (b) the contract
-- is a standard form contract; and (c) the contract is: (i) a financial product; or (ii) a contract for the supply, or possible
-- supply, of services that are financial services." s 12BI(1): s 12BF "does not apply to a term ... to the extent ... that: (a)
-- the term defines the main subject matter of the contract; or (b) ... sets the upfront price ...; or (c) ... is required, or
-- expressly permitted, by a law ...; ... (f) if the contract is an Insurance Contracts Act insurance contract--the term is a
-- transparent term and: (i) is disclosed at or before the time when the contract is made; and (ii) sets an amount of excess or
-- deductible". s 12BL(1): the Subdivision "does not apply to a contract that is the constitution of a company". s 12BK(1): a
-- contract alleged to be standard form is presumed so "unless another party ... proves otherwise" -- an input here.
DECLARE `My contract` HAS
    `is a consumer contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a small business contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a standard form contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a financial product or a contract for financial services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the constitution of a company` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the term of my contract void as unfair (ss 12BF(1), 12BI(1), 12BL(1))?
GIVEN `my contract` IS A `My contract` @desc What kind of contract it is
      `the term` IS A `The term` @desc The term in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the term void as unfair` IF
        (`my contract`'s `is a consumer contract` OR `my contract`'s `is a small business contract`)
    AND `my contract`'s `is a standard form contract`
    AND `my contract`'s `is a financial product or a contract for financial services`
    AND (NOT `my contract`'s `is the constitution of a company`)
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `defines the main subject matter of the contract`)
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `sets the upfront price`)
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `is required or expressly permitted by a law`)
    AND (NOT `the term`'s `is a transparent insurance excess disclosed before the contract`)
    AND `Is the term unfair` `the term`

§§ `ss 12CB, 12BB, 12DA, 12DJ -- conduct that may not be used on me`

-- s 12CB(1): "A person must not, in trade or commerce, in connection with: (a) the supply or possible supply of financial
-- services to a person; or (b) the acquisition or possible acquisition of financial services from a person; engage in conduct
-- that is, in all the circumstances, unconscionable." (2): it "does not apply to conduct that is engaged in only because the
-- person ... (a) institutes legal proceedings ...; or (b) refers to arbitration a dispute or claim".
@export Does the conduct towards me contravene the ban on unconscionable conduct (s 12CB)?
GIVEN `in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was in trade or commerce
      `in connection with supplying financial services to me or acquiring them from me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was in connection with financial services supplied to you or acquired from you
      `unconscionable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find it unconscionable in all the circumstances
      `only suing me or referring the dispute to arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was only starting legal proceedings or referring the dispute to arbitration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conduct contravene s 12CB` IF
        `in trade or commerce`
    AND `in connection with supplying financial services to me or acquiring them from me`
    AND `unconscionable in all the circumstances`
    AND (NOT `only suing me or referring the dispute to arbitration`)

-- s 12BB(1): "If: (a) a person makes a representation with respect to any future matter ...; and (b) the person does not have
-- reasonable grounds for making the representation; the representation is taken ... to be misleading." (2): the person is
-- "taken not to have had reasonable grounds ... unless evidence is adduced to the contrary".
DECLARE `The representation` HAS
    `misleading or deceptive, or likely to mislead or deceive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `about a future matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evidence was adduced of reasonable grounds and they were found` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is the representation made to me misleading (ss 12BB(1)-(2), 12DA(1))?
GIVEN `what was said` IS A `The representation` @desc What was said: whether misleading in fact, whether about the future, and whether reasonable grounds were shown
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the representation misleading` IF
        `what was said`'s `misleading or deceptive, or likely to mislead or deceive`
    OR  (    `what was said`'s `about a future matter`
         AND (NOT `what was said`'s `evidence was adduced of reasonable grounds and they were found`))

-- s 12DA(1): "A person must not, in trade or commerce, engage in conduct in relation to financial services that is misleading
-- or deceptive or is likely to mislead or deceive." (1A): conduct that contravenes Corporations Act s 670A (takeover document),
-- s 728 (fundraising document) or s 738Y (CSF offer document), or is "in relation to a disclosure document or statement within
-- the meaning of section 953A [or] 1022A of the Corporations Act", "does not contravene subsection (1)". s 12GB(1) makes the
-- other Subdivision D provisions offences "other than section 12DA", and s 12GBA(6)(b) leaves s 12DA out of the civil penalty
-- provisions: its remedy is damages (s 12GF) and the other orders.
@export Does the conduct contravene the ban on misleading or deceptive conduct in financial services (s 12DA)?
GIVEN `in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was in trade or commerce
      `in relation to financial services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was in relation to financial services (s 12BAB)
      `misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was misleading or deceptive, or likely to mislead or deceive (s 12BB counts)
      `covered by the Corporations Act document provisions in s 12DA(1A)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contravenes Corporations Act s 670A, 728 or 738Y, or concerns a s 953A or 1022A disclosure document or statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conduct contravene s 12DA` IF
        `in trade or commerce`
    AND `in relation to financial services`
    AND `misleading`
    AND (NOT `covered by the Corporations Act document provisions in s 12DA(1A)`)

-- s 12DJ(1): "A person contravenes this subsection if: (a) the person uses physical force or undue harassment or coercion; and
-- (b) the person uses such force, harassment or coercion in connection with the supply or possible supply of financial services
-- to a consumer, or the payment for financial services by a consumer." Gloss: whether harassment is "undue" is a court's
-- judgment and an input; s 12BC(4) presumes the person is a consumer unless the contrary is established.
@export May a collector or supplier use this conduct on me over financial services (s 12DJ)?
GIVEN `physical force, undue harassment or coercion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct is physical force, or harassment or coercion a court would find undue
      `in connection with supplying financial services to me or my paying for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is about supplying financial services to you or your paying for them, such as collecting a credit card debt
      `I am a consumer of those services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the services as a consumer (s 12BC; presumed unless shown otherwise)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the conduct contravene s 12DJ` IF
        `physical force, undue harassment or coercion`
    AND `in connection with supplying financial services to me or my paying for them`
    AND `I am a consumer of those services`

§§ `ss 12DL, 12DM, 12DMA -- cards and services I did not ask for`

-- s 12DL(1): "A person must not send another person ... a credit card or a debit card except in accordance with subsection
-- (2)." (2): it may be sent "(a) in pursuance of a request in writing by the person ... who will be under a liability to the
-- issuer ...; or (b) in renewal or replacement of, or in substitution for: (i) a card of the same kind previously sent ... in
-- pursuance of a request in writing ...; or (ii) a card of the same kind previously sent ... and used for a purpose for which
-- it was intended to be used." (3): only cards sent "by or on behalf of the issuer".
@export May the issuer send me this credit or debit card (s 12DL(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `I asked for it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (the person liable for the card) asked for it in writing
      `it renews or replaces a card of the same kind I asked for in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it renews, replaces or substitutes for a card of the same kind you asked for in writing
      `it renews or replaces a card of the same kind I have used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it renews, replaces or substitutes for a card of the same kind you have used as intended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the issuer send me the card` IF
        `I asked for it in writing`
    OR  `it renews or replaces a card of the same kind I asked for in writing`
    OR  `it renews or replaces a card of the same kind I have used`

-- s 12BA(1): "unsolicited financial services means financial services supplied to a person without any request made by the
-- person or on the person's behalf." s 12DMA: "If a person, in trade or commerce, supplies unsolicited financial services to
-- another person, the other person: (a) is not liable to make any payment for the services ...; and (b) is not liable for loss
-- or damage as a result of the supply". s 12DM(1): a person "must not, in trade or commerce, assert a right to payment ... for
-- unsolicited financial services", unless (1A) "the person had reasonable cause to believe that there was a right to payment".
@export Must I pay for financial services supplied to me (s 12DMA)?
GIVEN `I or someone for me requested them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or someone on your behalf, asked for the services
      `supplied in trade or commerce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a business supplied them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I pay for the services` IF
    NOT (`supplied in trade or commerce` AND (NOT `I or someone for me requested them`))

§§ `ss 12EB, 12EC, 12ED -- the warranties I get`

-- s 12ED(1): "In every contract for the supply of financial services by a person to a consumer in the course of a business,
-- there is an implied warranty that: (a) the services will be rendered with due care and skill; and (b) any materials supplied
-- in connection with those services will be reasonably fit for the purpose for which they are supplied." (3): "financial
-- services does not include ... services ... provided ... under a contract of insurance."
@export Do I have the implied warranty that the financial services will be rendered with due care and skill (s 12ED(1), (3))?
GIVEN `I acquired them as a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acquired the financial services as a consumer (s 12BC)
      `supplied in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supplier supplied them in the course of a business
      `provided under a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services are provided under a contract of insurance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the warranty of due care and skill` IF
        `I acquired them as a consumer`
    AND `supplied in the course of a business`
    AND (NOT `provided under a contract of insurance`)

-- s 12ED(2): where the consumer "makes known to the person: (i) any particular purpose for which the services are required; or
-- (ii) the result that he or she desires the services to achieve", there is a warranty that the services "will be reasonably
-- fit for that purpose or are of such a nature and quality that they might reasonably be expected to achieve that result,
-- except if the circumstances show that the consumer does not rely, or that it is unreasonable for him or her to rely, on the
-- person's skill or judgment."
@export Do I have the implied warranty that the services will be fit for the purpose I made known (s 12ED(2), (3))?
GIVEN `I have the due care and skill warranty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 12ED(1) applies to the contract (consumer, business supplier, not insurance)
      `I made known the purpose or result I wanted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the supplier, expressly or by implication, the purpose or result you wanted
      `I did not rely, or it was unreasonable to rely, on their skill or judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the circumstances show you did not rely, or could not reasonably rely, on the supplier's skill or judgment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the warranty of fitness for my purpose` IF
        `I have the due care and skill warranty`
    AND `I made known the purpose or result I wanted`
    AND (NOT `I did not rely, or it was unreasonable to rely, on their skill or judgment`)

-- s 12EB(1): a term "is void if it purports to exclude, restrict or modify or has the effect of excluding, restricting or
-- modifying: (a) the application of ... this Subdivision ...; (b) the exercise of a right conferred by such a provision; or (c)
-- any liability of the person for breach of a condition or warranty implied by such a provision." s 12EC(1): for "financial
-- services other than services of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use", a term is "not void
-- under section 12EB merely because" it limits liability to "(a) the supplying of the services again; or (b) the payment of the
-- cost of having the services supplied again", unless (2) the person supplied "establishes that it is not fair or reasonable
-- for the supplier to rely on that term".
@export Is the term excluding or limiting the implied warranties void (ss 12EB(1), 12EC)?
GIVEN `it excludes, restricts or modifies the warranties or liability for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term excludes, restricts or modifies the s 12ED warranties or liability for breaching them
      `the services are of a household kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services are of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic or household use
      `it only limits liability to supplying the services again or paying for that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term only limits liability to re-supplying the services or paying the cost of re-supply
      `I establish reliance on it is not fair or reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you show it is not fair or reasonable for the supplier to rely on the term
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the warranty exclusion void` IF
        `it excludes, restricts or modifies the warranties or liability for them`
    AND (   `the services are of a household kind`
         OR (NOT `it only limits liability to supplying the services again or paying for that`)
         OR `I establish reliance on it is not fair or reasonable`)

§§ `s 12GF -- what I can recover, and by when`

-- s 12GF(1): "A person who suffers loss or damage by conduct of another person that contravenes a provision of Subdivision BA
-- ..., Subdivision C ..., Subdivision D ... or Subdivision DA ... may recover the amount of the loss or damage by action against
-- that other person or against any person involved in the contravention." (2): "An action under subsection (1) may be
-- commenced within 6 years after the day on which the cause of action that relates to the conduct accrued." Dates as YYYYMMDD:
-- six years on is the number plus 60000 (a 29 February accrual would need a day's care; not modelled).
@export By when must I start an action for damages (s 12GF(2))?
GIVEN `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A NUMBER @desc The day your cause of action accrued, as YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By when must I sue for damages` IS `the day my cause of action accrued` PLUS 60000

-- s 12GF(1B): for "economic loss; or damage to property" caused by a contravention of s 12DA, where the claimant suffered it
-- "partly of the claimant's failure to take reasonable care" and the defendant "(i) did not intend to cause the loss or damage;
-- and (ii) did not fraudulently cause the loss or damage", the damages "are to be reduced to the extent to which the court
-- thinks just and equitable".
@export Can my damages for misleading conduct be reduced because I was careless too (s 12GF(1B))?
GIVEN `the claim is under s 12DA for economic loss or property damage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim is for economic loss or damage to property caused by misleading or deceptive conduct (s 12DA)
      `I partly failed to take reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the loss was partly the result of your own failure to take reasonable care
      `they intended or fraudulently caused the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other side intended to cause the loss, or caused it fraudulently
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my damages be reduced for my own carelessness` IF
        `the claim is under s 12DA for economic loss or property damage`
    AND `I partly failed to take reasonable care`
    AND (NOT `they intended or fraudulently caused the loss`)

§§ `ss 12GB, 12GBA, 12GBCA -- what I, or my company, can be made to pay`

-- s 12GBA(6): civil penalty provisions are "(aa) a provision of Subdivision BA; (a) a provision of Subdivision C; (b) a provision
-- of Subdivision D (other than section 12DA); (ba) a provision of Subdivision DA; (c) a provision of Subdivision GC."
DECLARE `The provision contravened` IS ONE OF
    `s 12BF(2A) or (2C), proposing or relying on an unfair term`
    `s 12CB, unconscionable conduct`
    `s 12DA, misleading or deceptive conduct`
    `s 12DJ, harassment or coercion`
    `s 12DL, an unsolicited card`
    `s 12DM, demanding payment for unsolicited services`

@export Is the provision a civil penalty provision (s 12GBA(6))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `The provision contravened` @desc Which provision was contravened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a civil penalty provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 12DA, misleading or deceptive conduct` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 12GB(1): a person commits an offence if the person contravenes, attempts to contravene, or is involved in a contravention
-- of, "a provision of Subdivision D (sections 12DA to 12DN), other than section 12DA". "Penalty: 2,000 penalty units."
@export Is contravening the provision an offence under s 12GB(1)?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `The provision contravened` @desc Which provision was contravened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a s 12GB offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 12DJ, harassment or coercion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 12DL, an unsolicited card` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 12DM, demanding payment for unsolicited services` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 12GBCA(1): for an individual, "the greater of: (a) 5,000 penalty units; and (b) if the Court can determine the benefit
-- derived and detriment avoided because of the contravention--that amount multiplied by 3." The value of a penalty unit is set
-- by Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA, not deposited: an input. A benefit the court cannot determine is entered as 0.
@export What is the most I can be ordered to pay as an individual for one contravention of a civil penalty provision (s 12GBCA(1))?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one Commonwealth penalty unit, in dollars (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA)
      `benefit derived and detriment avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit derived and detriment avoided because of the contravention, if the court can determine it; 0 if not
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be ordered to pay as an individual` IS
    IF (`benefit derived and detriment avoided` TIMES 3) GREATER THAN (5000 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`)
    THEN `benefit derived and detriment avoided` TIMES 3
    ELSE 5000 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

-- s 12GBCA(2): for a body corporate, "the greatest of: (a) 50,000 penalty units; and (b) ... [the benefit] multiplied by 3; and
-- (c) either: (i) 10% of the annual turnover of the body corporate for the 12-month period ending at the end of the month in
-- which the body corporate contravened ...; or (ii) if the amount worked out under subparagraph (i) is greater than an amount
-- equal to 2.5 million penalty units--2.5 million penalty units."
@export What is the most my company can be ordered to pay for one contravention of a civil penalty provision (s 12GBCA(2))?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one Commonwealth penalty unit, in dollars (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA)
      `benefit derived and detriment avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc The benefit derived and detriment avoided because of the contravention, if the court can determine it; 0 if not
      `annual turnover` IS A NUMBER @desc The company's turnover for the 12 months ending at the end of the month of the contravention, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my company can be ordered to pay` IS
    LET `limb a` = 50000 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
        `limb b` = `benefit derived and detriment avoided` TIMES 3
        `turnover share` = `annual turnover` TIMES 0.1
        `turnover cap` = 2500000 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
        `limb c` = IF `turnover share` GREATER THAN `turnover cap` THEN `turnover cap` ELSE `turnover share`
        `a or b` = IF `limb b` GREATER THAN `limb a` THEN `limb b` ELSE `limb a`
    IN IF `limb c` GREATER THAN `a or b` THEN `limb c` ELSE `a or b`

§§ `Part 3, ss 13, 19, 23, 30, 63, 68 -- what ASIC can make me do as founder`

-- s 13(1): ASIC "may make such investigation as it thinks expedient ... where it has reason to suspect that there may have been
-- committed: (a) a contravention of the corporations legislation"; (6): likewise where it suspects a contravention of Part 2
-- Division 2. s 19(2): ASIC "may, by written notice in the prescribed form given to the person, require the person: (a) to give
-- to ASIC all reasonable assistance ...; and (b) to appear ... for examination on oath or affirmation and to answer questions."
-- (3): the notice "must: (a) state the general nature of the matter ...; and (b) set out the effect of subsection 23(1) and
-- section 68." s 23(1): "The examinee's lawyer may be present at the examination". s 63(1): a person "must not intentionally or
-- recklessly fail to comply with a requirement made under: (a) section 19; ... (c) section 30 ...". "Penalty: 2 years
-- imprisonment." (5): not "to the extent that the person has a reasonable excuse". s 68(1): it "is not a reasonable excuse for a
-- person to refuse or fail: (a) to give information; or (b) to sign a record; or (c) to produce a book ... that [it] might tend
-- to incriminate the person or make the person liable to a penalty."
DECLARE `My excuse` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `it might incriminate me or expose me to a penalty`
    `another reasonable excuse`

@export Must I comply with ASIC's notice to attend an examination or produce books (ss 19, 30, 63, 68(1))?
GIVEN `I was given a written notice under s 19 or s 30` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC gave you a written notice under s 19 (examination) or s 30 (books of a body corporate)
      `my excuse` IS A `My excuse` @desc The reason, if any, you have for not complying
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I comply with ASIC's notice` IF
        `I was given a written notice under s 19 or s 30`
    AND (CONSIDER `my excuse`
         WHEN `another reasonable excuse` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 68(2)-(3): where, "before: (i) making an oral statement giving information; or (ii) signing a record", a person "(other than
-- a body corporate) claims that the statement ... might tend to incriminate the person or make the person liable to a penalty"
-- and it "might in fact" do so, the statement "is not admissible in evidence against the person in: (a) a criminal proceeding;
-- or (b) a proceeding for the imposition of a penalty; other than a proceeding in respect of: (c) ... the falsity of the
-- statement".
DECLARE `The later proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `a criminal or penalty proceeding about something else`
    `a proceeding about the falsity of my statement`
    `a civil proceeding that seeks no penalty`

@export Can what I said at the ASIC examination be used against me (s 68(2)-(3))?
GIVEN `I claimed privilege before answering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before answering or signing, you claimed the answer might incriminate you or expose you to a penalty
      `it might in fact incriminate me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the answer might in fact tend to incriminate you or expose you to a penalty
      `the proceeding` IS A `The later proceeding` @desc The proceeding in which it would be used
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my examination answer be used against me` IF
    IF `I claimed privilege before answering` AND `it might in fact incriminate me`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the proceeding`
          WHEN `a criminal or penalty proceeding about something else` THEN FALSE
          OTHERWISE TRUE)
    ELSE TRUE
